response:
@robjohn

What's the source of the quote, if you don't mind me asking? I've tried searching, but I'm not sure what to search for, and it's not in the book.

@robjohn

I don't know. I just heard it in a lecture, and it seemed like a great quote to me. I don't know where the lecturer got it from, either.

@robjohn

@robjohn

@robjohn

I don't know the source of the quote, but the book was written in the 2nd century, so it was written during the reign of Hadrian, who was a friend of Plutarch. It is unlikely that Plutarch would have known of the quote, but he may have written about it in his "Parallel Lives" (which I've never read).

@robjohn

I've read "Parallel Lives" (in the Penguin Classics translation) and it's a great book, but I don't think he ever mentions this quote.
